{"edition_id":"urn:uuid:35b4350d-7202-5d47-8b85-5262d7ca441c","id":"urn:uuid:711a13e6-4792-5d49-94f4-7ebd49b3ae6b","order":6,"protected_tokens":[],"record_type":"segment","rights_id":"urn:uuid:52a7c815-5b13-5f21-a52a-e7fa11238e07","schema_id":"ttna-segment-v1","schema_version":"1.0.0","semantic_slot":"paragraph","source_block_sha256":"f6dc35f9d5653040934e74737d98d23f65f9df28acab45496f481c53fff2db72","source_file_id":"urn:uuid:271e812b-1ccd-53ed-a402-07fe58709c8a","source_locale":"en-US","source_locator":{"end_line":503,"layout":"Standard","layout_ordinal":20,"start_line":491},"source_text":"Cocalc (Collaborative Calculation in the cloud) provides access to Octave, R, SageMath, \\SpecialChar LaTeX, C++, Julia, and a host of other kernels. Cocalc presents a much more robust environment, including classroom management features such as classes, posting and collecting assignments, collaborative editing, altogether a minimal set of tools for administering a course. They offer both free and paid account access. While they warn that running a free account may be slow, it also may suit your needs. It has been my experience that the free account requires substantial patience as connection issues and slow downs inevitably occur.","source_text_sha256":"8cfa223f44f287c2ad048f92c7f7997c7dcaf6e42f20ab90f5e6aa9794277fcf","translation_state":"source_frozen","unit_id":"urn:uuid:309948d3-a03e-5749-a53b-6f5dcf605717"}
{"from_id":"urn:uuid:ccdbeb43-f0eb-56a4-8834-7449d1fd7730","id":"urn:uuid:77a99c8d-9e1b-57a4-8076-f1f04026887d","record_type":"relation","relation":"translates","schema_id":"ttna-relation-v1","schema_version":"1.0.0","to_id":"urn:uuid:711a13e6-4792-5d49-94f4-7ebd49b3ae6b"}
{"edition_id":"urn:uuid:35b4350d-7202-5d47-8b85-5262d7ca441c","id":"urn:uuid:7b839644-f99b-5d56-96eb-04c4e461dfee","order":5,"protected_tokens":[],"record_type":"segment","rights_id":"urn:uuid:52a7c815-5b13-5f21-a52a-e7fa11238e07","schema_id":"ttna-segment-v1","schema_version":"1.0.0","semantic_slot":"paragraph","source_block_sha256":"f0dbc688ef8b6629cd4a3d463bd46fa2984d8e24c67f7f546541d55470ed1f1f","source_file_id":"urn:uuid:271e812b-1ccd-53ed-a402-07fe58709c8a","source_locale":"en-US","source_locator":{"end_line":489,"layout":"Standard","layout_ordinal":19,"start_line":481},"source_text":"Octave Online is designed as an Octave interface only and includes useful features for classroom use. Open a support ticket to inquire about setting up a course. The resulting course code gives instructors the ability to see student work spaces and collaborate in real time upon their enrollment in the course. Buckets allow an instructor to post read-only code for students to import into their accounts, making it easy to distribute code for labs or assignments.","source_text_sha256":"b1cb90663854ae73ba55caca1441a67e3ff1c942dde98315865e19a2b139f622","translation_state":"source_frozen","unit_id":"urn:uuid:309948d3-a03e-5749-a53b-6f5dcf605717"}
